 "method": "The county clerk's office e-mailed a scanned page of the county's township and commissioner district map on 2026-10-27. The scan is the county's copyrighted work and is not kept here; its SHA-256 is scanSha256. Its red district line was read off the page, the page having been lined up with the Census Bureau's county and township lines (569 points on the county's land edge, an affine fit, about 40 m to a half-resolution pixel), and each of the county's 888 Census 2020 blocks was put in the district holding most of it. Two stretches of the line are hidden under printed labels, about 2 km under the Ste. Genevieve township label and about 1.5 km under the city label, and were joined straight across. The clerk's polling place list puts Bloomsdale, Kinsey and Salem precincts whole in the First District and Coffman, New Offenburg, Ozora and St. Mary's whole in the Second; 12 blocks (38 people) the trace put on the other side of those precincts' 2020 lines were moved to match it.",
